<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Project 9 Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02533</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Project 9 Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>8b7d55a6-e10a-4b66-ac0e-43973d835f49</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this culminating project, you will synthesize methods of solving quadratic equations and graphing quadratic functions to answer questions about within a context. You will use tools learned throughout the unit to grapple with solving problems about a quadratic function that represents a context. Since this work requires using what you know to tackle an unfamiliar problem, you will need to make sense of problems and demonstrate perseverance.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Technology isn't required for this lesson, but there are opportunities for you to choose to use appropriate technology to solve problems.</para>
      <section id="sect-00002">
        <title>Project Activities</title>
        <list list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
          <item>Equations of Two Lines and a Curve</item>
          <item>Analyzing a Dive</item>
          <item>A Linear Function and a Quadratic Function</item>
          <item>Profit from a River Cruise</item>
        </list>
      </section>
      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title>Learning Targets</title>
        <para id="para-00003">When you finish this project, you will have demonstrated how to:</para>
        <list id="list-00002">
          <item>Interpret information about a quadratic function given its equation or a graph. </item>
          <item>Rewrite quadratic functions in different but equivalent forms of my choosing and use that form to solve problems. </item>
          <item>Decide which quadratic form to use depending on the questions being asked. </item>
        </list>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
